From: mho22 <yannick@capsules.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] Bind Omarchy's keys in sway

Omarchy 4 declares its key bindings in Hyprland Lua: the files in
default/hypr/bindings call o.bind from default/hypr/helpers.lua, and
hl.bind registers each binding with Hyprland. Kandelo ships sway,
which reads bindsym and bindcode lines.

omarchy-sway-bindings runs those files unchanged under a stub hl
table and prints one sway binding per Omarchy binding, after a comment
line that holds its description. A Hyprland dispatcher with a sway
command becomes that command. An exec binding is kept when its
programs are installed and, for omarchy-shell and omarchy-menu, when
--check says the call has an answer. Every other binding is skipped
with one line on stderr that names the reason.

omarchy-menu-keybindings reads sway's config and the files it
includes instead of hyprctl binds, takes each description from the
comment above its binding, and runs the selection with swaymsg.

